WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.735
-Adam, welcome.
Thank you so much.

00:00:02.735 --> 00:00:07.773
[ Mimicking applause ]

00:00:07.773 --> 00:00:10.477
Fake audience.
-Oh, thank you, thank you.

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:11.745
-Yeah.

00:00:11.745 --> 00:00:13.412
I'm so happy
that you're on my show.

00:00:13.412 --> 00:00:16.382
Thank you so much because I get
to congratulate you,

00:00:16.382 --> 00:00:18.251
kind of, over Zoom.

00:00:18.251 --> 00:00:21.287
Congratulations on being engaged
to be married.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:24.324
-Oh, thanks, Jimmy.
I appreciate it, yeah.

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:30.029
-Did the quarantine put a stop
to the planning at all?

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:32.165
-Well, neither of us
are, like, huge planners.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:36.369
So, we kind of didn't
start planning

00:00:36.369 --> 00:00:37.737
until the quarantine hit

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:40.139
and we're like, "We should
probably get on this."

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:43.109
And then realized that, like,
everything is pushed

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:44.443
like a solid year and a half.

00:00:44.443 --> 00:00:46.046
So now, I didn't want

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.614
to be involved
with any of the planning.

00:00:48.614 --> 00:00:53.485
I wrote a post to Chloe saying,
"Look, we got engaged,"

00:00:53.485 --> 00:00:57.490
and in the post I wrote,
"Have fun planning the wedding.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.259
I'll see you
at the cake tasting,"

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:00.727
and everyone is like,
"That's cute."

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:03.162
And I'm like, "That's real."
I plan on not being involved.

00:01:03.162 --> 00:01:05.798
-[ Laughs ]
"I'm just gonna show up."

00:01:05.798 --> 00:01:09.369
-Yeah, I'm like, "I'm just here,
put on the tux, I do."

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:12.671
And now there's
no getting around it

00:01:12.671 --> 00:01:15.041
because she'll be like, "What do
you think of these flowers?"

00:01:15.041 --> 00:01:16.642
and I can't be like, "I'm busy."

00:01:16.642 --> 00:01:18.210
And she's like,
"You're not busy.

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:20.880
You're watching season six
of 'The Sopranos.'"

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.649
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:23.649 --> 00:01:24.684
-Which is good.

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:27.219
-Which is great, by the way.

00:01:27.219 --> 00:01:29.389
I want to get into
all these things because --

00:01:29.389 --> 00:01:31.791
I want to get into "Bad Ideas"
because I think --

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:34.593
Has your confidence
increased now

00:01:34.593 --> 00:01:38.398
because of your show that's on
Quibi, "Bad Ideas"?

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:42.802
Like, now that you want --
You're like a daredevil now?

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:45.271
-Yeah.
It's a weird thing.

00:01:45.271 --> 00:01:49.208
It's definitely kind of stuff
that in my normal regular life

00:01:49.208 --> 00:01:50.610
I would never do.

00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:53.412
We went up the Amazon
and I swam with piranhas,

00:01:53.412 --> 00:01:55.481
and we drove -- I drove a truck

00:01:55.481 --> 00:01:57.349
on one of the world's
most dangerous roads,

00:01:57.349 --> 00:01:59.586
things that I normally
wouldn't do.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:02.588
There's definitely an element
of danger to the show that,

00:02:02.588 --> 00:02:08.294
in hindsight, I was like, "Oh,
uh, maybe if we do a season 2,

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:11.030
I'm a little more cautious."

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.599
-Yeah, you're like, "I've never
had a fried egg before.

00:02:13.599 --> 00:02:15.634
That would be
kind of cool, right?

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:18.571
That's a bad idea."

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.840
-It's a bad idea.

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:22.075
-"This is not gonna
be good at all

00:02:22.075 --> 00:02:23.843
if I eat two
of these McMuffins."

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.745
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:28.547
"I'm a wild man. Indigestion.
Kill me now."

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:31.517
-Dude, "Wild Man with
Adam Devine" is another one.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:33.786
That's a different show.

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:37.957
-Yeah, how many fruit I can eat
out of this fruit tray.

00:02:37.957 --> 00:02:40.226
-Oh, man, he's nuts!
No spoilers.

00:02:40.226 --> 00:02:42.428
-"He's wild,
and he's dipping it in yogurt!

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:43.596
This guy's insane!"

00:02:43.596 --> 00:02:44.797
-Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:02:44.797 --> 00:02:48.668
"Can I show this on TV?"
-Too much dairy.

00:02:48.668 --> 00:02:52.638
-Did you end up getting hurt
at all doing these things?

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:54.473
-I did -- Yeah, so, I did one

00:02:54.473 --> 00:02:59.111
with Blake Anderson
from "Workaholics."

00:02:59.111 --> 00:03:03.449
And we did a demolition derby,
and that one was nuts, Jimmy,

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:04.851
'cause I didn't know how --

00:03:04.851 --> 00:03:07.286
They, like, literally taught us
how to drive stick, like,

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:09.322
right before we get in
this demolition derby.

00:03:09.322 --> 00:03:13.225
So, we did one that was like
a double decker where two cars

00:03:13.225 --> 00:03:15.294
that are, like, welded on
top of each other.

00:03:15.294 --> 00:03:19.866
And Blake was in charge
of the gas and the brakes

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.034
and I was in charge
of the steering.

00:03:22.034 --> 00:03:24.737
And we were doing great.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:27.439
But then we -- it was like --
we're in first place

00:03:27.439 --> 00:03:29.475
and really, for whatever reason

00:03:29.475 --> 00:03:30.877
this just worked
for the two of us,

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.978
but you couldn't hear,
so we're screaming.

00:03:32.978 --> 00:03:36.582
I'm like, "Brake, brake!"
and he's like, "Gas?"

00:03:36.582 --> 00:03:38.417
And we took a corner
too quickly.

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:41.620
-The opposite of brake. It
doesn't even rhyme with brake!

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.289
-It doesn't even sound close!

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:46.592
And we flipped over,
and I was at the top.

00:03:46.592 --> 00:03:50.563
So it came down and, like,
a full-on surplap, surplap!

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.599
And I was like -- saw stars.

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:55.768
I cracked a rib.
-No!

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:58.103
-My neck was all messed up.
Yeah.

00:03:58.103 --> 00:04:00.773
And then, like, from there,
they pulled us out

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:02.842
and then they're like,
"Are you good?"

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.377
And I'm like, "I think so."

00:04:04.377 --> 00:04:05.577
And they're like,
"Can you do that?"

00:04:05.577 --> 00:04:06.779
And I'm like, "Uh..."

00:04:06.779 --> 00:04:08.013
And they're like,
"You don't have a concussion.

00:04:08.013 --> 00:04:09.248
You're good. Next race."

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:10.883
And I'm like...

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:12.051
-Wow!

00:04:12.051 --> 00:04:14.787
-Yeah, and that's just
one of the episodes.

00:04:14.787 --> 00:04:16.588
It truly was insane.

00:04:16.588 --> 00:04:20.759
Rebel Wilson and I
did an action stunt episode.

00:04:20.759 --> 00:04:23.862
-Reunited.
-Yeah, we were reunited.

00:04:23.862 --> 00:04:25.298
And it feels so good.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:29.802
And we always talk about how
we're known as comedy people,

00:04:29.802 --> 00:04:33.840
but we want to be
some cool action heroes.

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:34.907
You know?

00:04:34.907 --> 00:04:36.476
-All comedians
want to be James Bond.

00:04:36.476 --> 00:04:39.045
-We all want to be something
we're obviously not.

00:04:39.045 --> 00:04:42.682
And I'm like, "I'm a cool action
hero" and she's the same way.

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.016
And so I was like,
"We should do something

00:04:44.016 --> 00:04:46.518
where we get to do
a ton of cool stunts."

00:04:46.518 --> 00:04:51.557
And so she -- We're, like,
at a wild Western theme place,

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:56.796
and she like -- We get in a big
bar fight and she shoots me

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:58.064
and I run up the stairs

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.565
and I'm looking
for a way to escape

00:04:59.565 --> 00:05:03.269
and she comes outside and she
shoots me from the street

00:05:03.269 --> 00:05:08.207
and I fall like four stories
into some cardboard boxes,

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:11.944
and I told the stunt guys
this idea,

00:05:11.944 --> 00:05:14.113
and they're like, "Cool,
so when you get up there,

00:05:14.113 --> 00:05:16.115
we'll do a Texas switch

00:05:16.115 --> 00:05:17.449
and you'll flip
with the real stunt guy

00:05:17.449 --> 00:05:18.684
and he'll fall into the boxes."

00:05:18.684 --> 00:05:21.354
I'm like, "No, that's the whole
point of the show

00:05:21.354 --> 00:05:23.055
is I'm going to fall
onto the boxes.

00:05:23.055 --> 00:05:24.523
And they're like, "Well, that's
a really bad idea,"

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:25.925
and I'm like, "Exactly!"

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.593
-That's the name of the show!

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:30.663
-"That's the name of the show!"

00:05:30.663 --> 00:05:32.498
-I want to show --
-It's on Quibi now.

00:05:32.498 --> 00:05:34.300
-I want to show a clip.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.268
This is from the demolition
derby episode.

00:05:36.268 --> 00:05:39.305
Take a look at this.
-Oh, cool.

00:05:39.305 --> 00:05:40.572
-Slow down when we get into

00:05:40.572 --> 00:05:42.375
the turns
because this thing can tip.

00:05:42.375 --> 00:05:45.010
-All gas, no brake.
-What?

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:46.912
-All gas, no brake.
-No!

00:05:46.912 --> 00:05:53.385 line:0%
♪♪

00:05:53.385 --> 00:05:55.021
-Now we're cooking, baby!

00:05:57.155 --> 00:05:58.991
-Let's make a run
for the jewels.

00:05:58.991 --> 00:06:05.998 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:05.998 --> 00:06:13.005 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:13.005 --> 00:06:15.774
-Ugh.
-Hey, Adam, you good?

00:06:15.774 --> 00:06:20.046
-I feel like I got hit
in the head with a baseball bat.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:21.480
-We're okay!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:21.480 --> 00:06:25.584
-We didn't die!

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:27.487
-We had it too, boy.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.256
-My thanks to Adam Devine.

00:06:30.256 --> 00:06:33.726
Check out "Bad Ideas
with Adam Devine" on Quibi.

00:06:33.726 --> 00:06:35.260
Chronixx performs for us next.

00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:36.395
Stick around, everybody.

00:06:36.395 --> 00:06:38.230
Good luck on
the wedding planning.

00:06:38.230 --> 00:06:39.899
-Yeah, thanks, Jimmy.
See ya, man.

